                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Review: Drift Zone   [/h1]\n[list]\n[*][h1]Graphics / Audio :[/h1]\nGame was developed by a smaller studio called Awesome Industries. Considering the game was developed by a small studio i have to say that it does look good enough where you get a good feeling about it visually with sharp textures and good particles ( effects ). Keep in mind that the textures do get blurry when drifting which i am not a big fan of. Lighting is decent enough too. Sounds aren't the best as they all sound pretty generic and boring with subpar quality. Still it is a pretty ok looking game in my opinion.\n\n[b][ 6,5 out of 10 ][/b]\n\n[*][h1]Gameplay :[/h1]\nThis is a so called Drifting Game and to some extent it does achieve that genre name. Sadly it does have a lot of flaws, the steering feels unresponsive as you can barely feel or see when the car is starting to lose control, gamepad / Steering wheel  options and compatibility are pretty bad as i had problems with a controller ( XBOX 1) and i couldn't even use a steering wheel ( Thrustmaster T150 ), It does have no unique gamemodes which makes it feel pretty blank and \"slim\", and no online available ( yet ). Costumization is pretty good and you have the ability to tune and upgrade your car which doesn't make it look that bad.\n\n[b][ 5,5 out of 10 ][/b]\n\n[*][h1]Story :[/h1]\n-\n[b][- ][/b]\n\n[*][h1]Multiplayer :[/h1]\n-\n\n[b][ - ][/b]\n\n[*][h1]Performance :[/h1]\nLooking at the Recommended requirements i was a little worried that the game would ran poor on a Mid Range PC ( AMD FX 6300 & GTX 760 ) but it was actually easily running it on Maxed out graphics with more than 60 fps. Obviously runs easily on High End Pcs ( Intel i7 4790k & GTX 1070 ). I am not 100% sure but there is a chance that it runs on weaker systems like Laptops ( Intel i5 5200U & Intel HD 5500 ). Still it was running great with no bugs or other problems.\n\n[b][ 9 out of 10 ][/b]\n\n[*][h1]Price :[/h1]\nFor 6,99 Eur. it isnt expensive but there is not enough content or amazing gameplay when compared to other drifting games.\n\n\nNot Recommended as the game needs some more updates in order to feel great. ( It does have potential but it is not great atm as it still needs some work. )\nI will change the review to positive when it will get updated and become better.\n\n[table]\n[th] If you like my Review be sure to Join[url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/indiepromo] IndiePromo[/url]![/th]",
